# The task classes the gateway exposes. One row per class; `|`-delimited.
#
#   name | required env keys (space-separated) | fallback classes (comma-separated) | probe URL
#
# A class is LIVE when every required key is set and its probe (if any)
# answers. Anything else is a hard stop at start time unless the operator
# names the class in `--allow-missing`.
#
# Fallbacks never cross DOWN into a cheaper class. `frontier` degrades to
# `frontier-light` — still Anthropic, still frontier-grade judgment — and
# never to `cheap`, because a silent downgrade of a code review or a migration
# to a flash model is indistinguishable from a correct answer until it is not.
# `cheap` and `local` degrade into each other freely: same trust tier, and an
# outage there should not stall a label census.
#
# Which work goes to which class is the routing policy table in
# docs/agent-gateway.md. Keep the two in step.
frontier|ANTHROPIC_API_KEY|frontier-light|
frontier-light|ANTHROPIC_API_KEY||
cheap|GEMINI_API_KEY|local|
local||cheap|http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/tags
